===Verb===
{{en-verb|past2=daylit}}

# To expose to daylight
#* {{RQ:Wells Time Machine|[http://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/35/pg35-images.html Chapter 7]||{{...}} the Morlocks, subterranean for innumerable generations, had come at last to find the '''daylit''' surface intolerable.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1953|author=w:C. S. Lewis|title=w:The Silver Chair|publisher=Collins|year_published=1998|chapter=15
|passage={{...}} she was not looking at the '''daylit''', sunny world which she so wanted to see.}}
# {{lb|en|architecture}} To provide sources of natural illumination such as [[skylight]]s or windows.
# To allow light in, as by opening [[drapes]].
# {{lb|en|landscaping|civil engineering}} To run a drainage pipe to an opening from which its contents can drain away naturally.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To gain exposure to the open.
#: {{ux|en|The seam of coal '''daylighted''' at a cliff by the river.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1964|month=October|title=Letters: A US lesson in high-capacity freight stock|journal=Modern Railways|page=233|text=Tunnels were enlarged or '''daylighted''' and clearances generally greatly improved.}}

